WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.200
-How are you? How's the fam?

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:04.000
-Everybody is really good.
Thanks for asking.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:05.901
-Yeah. You're married to
the very funny Melissa McCarthy.

00:00:05.901 --> 00:00:07.834
We've talked about this
on the show.

00:00:07.834 --> 00:00:09.567
You have --
You have two kids, right?

00:00:09.567 --> 00:00:11.033
-That's right.
We have two girls, yeah.

00:00:11.033 --> 00:00:14.033
-Do they realize
that their parents are funny?

00:00:14.033 --> 00:00:15.868
[ Light laughter ]
-They do not. They do not.

00:00:15.868 --> 00:00:17.067
[ Laughter ]

00:00:17.067 --> 00:00:19.067
Yeah, we try to do bits
for them, Jimmy.

00:00:19.067 --> 00:00:21.734
And usually,
it's met with a stone face

00:00:21.734 --> 00:00:23.801
and then, eventually, like,
"Please stop."

00:00:23.801 --> 00:00:25.067
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, really?

00:00:25.067 --> 00:00:26.501
-What we decided is because

00:00:26.501 --> 00:00:28.400
they don't like our bits and
they don't think we're funny,

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:31.100
is that we go the other way.

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:32.300
So, we say, "Okay, fine.

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:34.100
Would you rather
that we're bankers?"

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:35.868
And so, we have these characters
that we play

00:00:35.868 --> 00:00:38.033
that are the bankers.

00:00:38.033 --> 00:00:39.934
And the bankers
are very serious,

00:00:39.934 --> 00:00:41.534
and it becomes much more like,

00:00:41.534 --> 00:00:45.300
"Georgette, I hope school
was interesting today.

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:47.501
[ Laughter ]
"Would you please tell me

00:00:47.501 --> 00:00:49.934
the longest portion
of your day?"

00:00:49.934 --> 00:00:51.434
[ Laughter ]

00:00:51.434 --> 00:00:53.434
And finally, we do it long
enough, and they'll be like,

00:00:53.434 --> 00:00:54.667
"Okay, do your stupid dancing.
Whatever."

00:00:54.667 --> 00:00:56.100
-"Go back to the other --
dumb characters," yeah.

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:57.167
-Let's talk about your new show.

00:00:57.167 --> 00:00:59.167
It's called
"God's Favorite Idiot."

00:00:59.167 --> 00:01:02.133
God, that made me laugh,
just hearing that title.

00:01:02.133 --> 00:01:03.300
Can you set up
what the show is about?

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:05.234
I think it's a great idea.
-Sure.

00:01:05.234 --> 00:01:09.434
It's really -- It's just about
this unassuming guy named Clark.

00:01:09.434 --> 00:01:11.167
I play Clark.

00:01:11.167 --> 00:01:14.000
And he is --

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:15.801
he is a messenger of God.

00:01:15.801 --> 00:01:18.100
And he doesn't -- he doesn't
know what's happening to him

00:01:18.100 --> 00:01:20.734
or why what's happening to him
is happening to him.

00:01:20.734 --> 00:01:23.334
And basically, it's a look --
it's a comedy.

00:01:23.334 --> 00:01:25.334
And it's a look at
what would happen if, like,

00:01:25.334 --> 00:01:28.067
a doofus was chosen
to save the world.

00:01:28.067 --> 00:01:31.100
-I want to ask you about this
'cause I know, in the show,

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:33.934
you're in -- fall in love
with Melissa's character.

00:01:33.934 --> 00:01:35.267
We were talking
a little bit backstage,

00:01:35.267 --> 00:01:38.968
and you said, "Oh, dude,
the proposal was terrible."

00:01:38.968 --> 00:01:41.234
-I really --
I knew she was the one.

00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:43.100
I knew I loved her very much
and I wanted to marry her.

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:46.434
So -- But I didn't have
all the things.

00:01:46.434 --> 00:01:48.100
And, you know,
I couldn't take her

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:50.067
to a top of a mountain
or anything.

00:01:50.067 --> 00:01:51.868
And, also,
she doesn't like mountains,

00:01:51.868 --> 00:01:53.467
so that would have been stupid
in the first place.

00:01:53.467 --> 00:01:54.834
-Yeah, of course.
So take the mountain off.

00:01:54.834 --> 00:01:57.701
-Yeah. No mountains.
So I'm like, okay,

00:01:57.701 --> 00:02:00.567
well, her favorite place to get
bagels is from this place.

00:02:00.567 --> 00:02:03.334
And her favorite place in town
is our back porch

00:02:03.334 --> 00:02:05.000
'cause she had
just remodeled this house,

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:06.334
and the back porch was lovely.

00:02:06.334 --> 00:02:07.467
So, I've got the bagels.

00:02:07.467 --> 00:02:09.200
And I'm kind of starting
to freak out.

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:10.834
And I'm like, "Hey, would --
Uh, Melissa, would you like

00:02:10.834 --> 00:02:12.467
to go to the back porch,
please?"

00:02:12.467 --> 00:02:13.934
[ Laughter ]
And she's like,

00:02:13.934 --> 00:02:16.267
"Oh, boy, he's getting
a little weird on me."

00:02:16.267 --> 00:02:18.467
I'm about to, you know,
drop to a knee,

00:02:18.467 --> 00:02:21.767
and bang, bang, bang
on the door.

00:02:21.767 --> 00:02:22.801
"Who's that?"

00:02:22.801 --> 00:02:24.133
"Oh, it's -- it's --

00:02:24.133 --> 00:02:25.400
it's a contractor.

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:27.868
He's here to install
a vintage toilet.

00:02:27.868 --> 00:02:29.200
[ Laughter ]

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:31.100
-Oh, so you can't ask her then
'cause you're like --

00:02:31.100 --> 00:02:33.334
-No. Because there's a guy
messing around with the toilet.

00:02:33.334 --> 00:02:35.334
Like, I couldn't be
the toilet proposal, so --

00:02:35.334 --> 00:02:36.767
-No. What do you do?
You have the bagels.

00:02:36.767 --> 00:02:37.968
-So, I've got the bagels.

00:02:37.968 --> 00:02:39.634
And so now
we're just eating bagels.

00:02:39.634 --> 00:02:41.734
And -- And it's just weird.

00:02:41.734 --> 00:02:44.033
And so now,
I take her to a dog park.

00:02:44.033 --> 00:02:46.167
Because I'm like,
"Plan B, a dog park."

00:02:46.167 --> 00:02:47.834
And then, I'm like --
I don't want to --

00:02:47.834 --> 00:02:49.567
you know,
we can't do this at a dog park.

00:02:49.567 --> 00:02:50.767
Finally --
-Do you have a dog?

00:02:50.767 --> 00:02:52.300
-Yeah, we do.
At least we have a dog.

00:02:52.300 --> 00:02:53.300
-Alright, good.
-Yes.

00:02:53.300 --> 00:02:54.667
-Alright.
-No, I think --

00:02:54.667 --> 00:02:55.868
-That helps. I didn't know.
I didn't know how weird --

00:02:55.868 --> 00:02:56.934
-Just randomly take her
to a dog -- No, no.

00:02:56.934 --> 00:02:58.801
-We're taking the plumber
to a dog park.

00:02:58.801 --> 00:03:00.667
Alright.
What's happening?

00:03:00.667 --> 00:03:02.367
Wow.
-So, finally, it's like --

00:03:02.367 --> 00:03:03.601
I'm freaking out.

00:03:03.601 --> 00:03:05.901
My blood pressure
is just skyrocketing all day.

00:03:05.901 --> 00:03:07.968
And the guy leaves.

00:03:07.968 --> 00:03:09.968
Melissa is watching
an autopsy show...

00:03:09.968 --> 00:03:11.267
[ Laughter ]

00:03:11.267 --> 00:03:13.901
...and playing like
a handheld "Tetris" game

00:03:13.901 --> 00:03:15.501
that you would play with --
you know,

00:03:15.501 --> 00:03:17.067
I don't know -- 20 years --
-Autopsy show?

00:03:17.067 --> 00:03:20.434
-Yes. And I literally -- I'm so
Jacked up and I'm freaked out.

00:03:20.434 --> 00:03:23.300
And I just rush at her and go,
"Melissa, will you marry me!"

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:26.667
[ Laughter ]
-And...

00:03:26.667 --> 00:03:27.968
-And she did --

00:03:27.968 --> 00:03:29.601
Actually,
she technically never said yes.

00:03:29.601 --> 00:03:31.033
[ Laughter ]

00:03:31.033 --> 00:03:32.801
She was just,
I think, so freaked out.

00:03:32.801 --> 00:03:34.701
She gave me a hug, and it seemed
like everything was cool,

00:03:34.701 --> 00:03:35.801
and we did get married.
-Ah.

00:03:35.801 --> 00:03:37.133
You've been married ever since.
-Yeah.

00:03:37.133 --> 00:03:38.434
-Congratulations on that.
-Thank you very much.

00:03:38.434 --> 00:03:39.267
That's a beautiful story.
-Thank you.

00:03:39.267 --> 00:03:40.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:40.334 --> 00:03:42.767
[ Laughter ]

00:03:42.767 --> 00:03:44.601
-I love it when you come on.

00:03:44.601 --> 00:03:45.601
You guys make a great team.

00:03:45.601 --> 00:03:46.968
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:03:46.968 --> 00:03:48.734
Here's Ben Falcone
and Melissa McCarthy

00:03:48.734 --> 00:03:51.133
in "God's Favorite Idiot."
Take a look at this.

00:03:51.133 --> 00:03:54.501
-I just was wondering, um, if
you'd like to go out sometime?

00:03:54.501 --> 00:03:56.100
But with -- But with me, though?

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:58.567
Um, I -- I ask because I think
you're really nice

00:03:58.567 --> 00:04:01.100
and you're, um, you're very --
you're very lovely.

00:04:01.100 --> 00:04:03.000
Um, and you're --
you're very bold.

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:04.334
And, um, also,

00:04:04.334 --> 00:04:06.868
in a non-harassment way
in the workplace,

00:04:06.868 --> 00:04:08.167
I wanted just to say
that I think

00:04:08.167 --> 00:04:09.634
you're not ugly...
-Ohh.

00:04:09.634 --> 00:04:11.767
-[ Breathes sharply ]
...in an attractiveness way.

00:04:11.767 --> 00:04:14.534
Ohh, that's not it.
That is not it.

00:04:14.534 --> 00:04:16.734
-You basically
just called me a dude.

00:04:16.734 --> 00:04:18.167
And an ugly dude.

00:04:18.167 --> 00:04:19.868
-Perhaps we could imagine
that I'm doing this better.

00:04:19.868 --> 00:04:21.901
Could we pretend, perhaps,
that I'm a Brad Pitt?

00:04:21.901 --> 00:04:22.767
I don't know Brad Pitt.

00:04:22.767 --> 00:04:24.434
I should call him Bradley Pitt.

00:04:24.434 --> 00:04:26.334
Could we pretend
that I'm Bradley Pitt

00:04:26.334 --> 00:04:27.601
doing this how he would do it,

00:04:27.601 --> 00:04:29.501
like Bradley Pitt is suddenly
inside of my body?

00:04:29.501 --> 00:04:31.567
-Oh. That's -- okay.

00:04:31.567 --> 00:04:32.934
-Nope. No.
No, Bradley Pitt --

00:04:32.934 --> 00:04:34.334
-It's a different visual.
-[ Clears throat ]

00:04:34.334 --> 00:04:35.667
He's not -- yeah.
He's not there.

00:04:35.667 --> 00:04:38.634
And that just -- let's wipe
our slate clean of that.

00:04:38.634 --> 00:04:40.701
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:40.701 --> 00:04:42.901
-Ben Falcone, everybody.

00:04:42.901 --> 00:04:46.634
"God's Favorite Idiot" begins
streaming on Netflix June 15th.

